+/* ── Lockstep workers (xbox_LockstepSet) ─────────────────────
+ *
+ * For a game that puts guest memory back in time (rollback netcode): the
+ * worker threads must not run on the host's schedule, or a rollback rewinds
+ * memory under a worker that is half way through changing it, and the replay
+ * of a tick does not see the same worker work as the first run did.
+ *
+ * While lockstep is on, a spawned guest thread parks at every sleep and wait
+ * (ordinals 99, 158, 159, 233, 234, 235) and runs only when the main thread
+ * grants it a turn (xbox_LockstepPump): one worker at a time, in the order
+ * they were spawned, each until it parks again. In a turn a sleep returns at
+ * once and a wait looks at its objects once (zero timeout); a wait that finds
+ * nothing signalled parks again (an INFINITE one) or returns STATUS_TIMEOUT
+ * (a finite one, so a polling loop goes round once per turn). Between turns
+ * every worker is parked at a kernel call, which is the state a game can save
+ * and restore guest memory in.
